  "full_text": "So, entertain God and your ass will follow. So, sounds like construction, doesn't it? What are they doing? It's a digger. There's a digger. So, well, I wonder if God is doing construction on the earth. Is God still deep creation? Of course he does. Maybe not. Maybe he's like, no, fuck it. Wouldn't you like to know the numbers on... how much effort God puts into creation every day, how much effort he puts into killing niggers, doing justice. Hey, I think that's new. I don't think that was there. So they discover a new species every once in a while. There was a really cool black neon purple frog in about 2004 they discovered. Google black purple neon frog. Anyway, so I wonder what we could expect. What kind of creation can God do? I don't know. You know, they unearth artifacts and stuff like Jonestown bush. When he was there, they unearthed the scabbard. Anyway, pick a winner. God knows our limits, but you, O Lord, are a God merciful and gracious, slow to anger and abundant in loving kindness and truth. Our Lord understands our limits. He realizes our struggles. He knows how much pressure we can take. He knows what measures of grace and mercy and strength we will require. He knows how we're put together. Frankly, His expectations are not nearly as unrealistic as ours. When we don't live up to the agenda we have set, we feel like He's going to dump a truckload of judgment on us. but that will not happen. So why do we fear it could?",
